=== (6) continuous multi-shift mixing (title hole), SPECTRAL level only: partner relation along a line ===
  test: every nonzero eigenvalue g of Pi(t) with |g| > eps has g + s in spec Pi(t+q) for some s in Sigma0(q) (forward direction checked);
  AND (local-affine step, vR17-8:15) the increment of every eigenvalue that is separated on [t-q, t+q] lies in Sigma0(q)
  q=1e-02: zigzag {+tri,-tri} (R17-8 control): worst defect / q = 0.497;   touching candidate {tri, +pi/2, -pi/2}: worst defect / q = 0.319
  q=1e-03: zigzag {+tri,-tri} (R17-8 control): worst defect / q = 0.372;   touching candidate {tri, +pi/2, -pi/2}: worst defect / q = 0.314
  (defect/q ~ 1 = fails; ~0 = passes the SPECTRAL relation. Passing is necessary only: the intertwiner identity (*),
   W1 symmetric stress and the redshift test are NOT checked here.)

=== (7) orientation monodromy of the line field span(d) around a conical point in a transverse slice (Lemma X2) ===
  track a continuous unit field n || d along a small circle (sign chosen for continuity, through sign-flip zeros);
  monodromy = n(2pi).n(0) (+1 trivial, -1 branched cover). Also count the sign-flip crossings.
  d=(x^2, xy, 0)            [A-line x=0 through a conical point]: monodromy +1.000000; sign-flip crossings 2
  d=((y^2-x^3)x,(y^2-x^3)y,0) [cusp A-curve through a conical pt]: monodromy +1.000000; sign-flip crossings 2
  d=(x(x-y)(x+2y), x y (x-y), y^3) [mixed, cubic]: monodromy +1.000000; sign-flip crossings 0
  d=(x y, x^2 - y^2, x^3)   [conical only]: monodromy +1.000000; sign-flip crossings 0
  d=(x, y, 0)               [Weyl-like line, conical only]: monodromy +1.000000; sign-flip crossings 0
  40 random laws d = (linear form) x (random quadratic+cubic vector): min monodromy +1.000000; flip counts [2]
  CONTROL (NOT analytic: d = (y, r - x, 0), zero set = one half-line): monodromy -1.000000; sign-flip crossings 1  -> the tracker detects a branched (odd) case when one exists
